>>
>>Of course, as somebody just pointed out, a ring of regeneration or 
>>conflict will do just as well if you have one...

>so if i were to wear rings of regeneration and hunger at the same time, 
>would i get hungry twice as fast?

No, not really, although it would have a cumulative effect.

Normal food consumption is 1 unit per move, with an extra 1 in 10 for both
hunger and regen (and conflict). So with both rings you would consume 12 units
every 10 moves, instead of 11 with one ring.

In theory if you were able to get intrinsic hunger, regeneration, and conflict,
you were wearing an amulet and possesed the Amulet of Yendor, and two charged
rings (eg., +1 ring of protection, +2 ring of increase damage or whatever),
and were stressed or more then you would get hungry at a rate of 18 units per
10 moves, which I believe is the maximum possible.

